BT /F1 14 Tf 72 760 Td (1 Why leave recurrence behind) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 738 Td (Recurrence ties each step of a computation to the one before it, which is why a recurrent model) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 724 Td (cannot be spread across accelerators as freely as a feed-forward one.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 710 Td (A weight for a value comes from comparing a query against that value's key; the answer is the) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 696 Td (weighted sum of the values. Nothing in that operation depends on the order in which positions) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 682 Td (are read.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 668 Td (This report makes the case that a sequence model does not need a recurrent path, and) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 654 Td (describes one whose whole computation is a stack of weighted-key lookups.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 640 Td (The result is shorter to implement and cheaper to parallelise, and on the tests below it needs) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 626 Td (fewer operations than the recurrent baselines to reach the same quality.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 72 780 Td (Weighted Keys, Shorter Paths) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 297 36 Td (2) Tj ET
endstream
endobj
