BT /F1 14 Tf 72 760 Td (2 The block) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 738 Td (The shape is the usual encoder-decoder one: a source sentence goes in, a target sentence) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 724 Td (comes out, and both sides repeat the same block.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 710 Td (Each stack holds seven identical blocks.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 696 Td (A block carries two sub-layers ó a weighted-key layer and a position-wise feed-forward layer ó) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 682 Td (each with a residual path and a normalisation step around it.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 668 Td (A residual connection [1] wraps each sub-layer, and layer normalisation [2] follows it.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 654 Td (Both the encoder and the decoder are built from self-attention and position-wise feed-forward) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 640 Td (layers.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 626 Td (The decoder adds a third sub-layer, so that its masked lookup can consult what the encoder) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 612 Td (produced.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 598 Td (Masking, plus the one-position shift on the output side, keeps each prediction to positions) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 584 Td (already produced.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 72 780 Td (Weighted Keys, Shorter Paths) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 297 36 Td (3) Tj ET
endstream
